These are the files that can be used with turbinesFoam to model a NACA0018 airfoil. The files that have a single Re value in the title are for the single Re models, but it is highly recommended that you use the multiRe model instead (which automatically shifts the Re values based on the speed/turbulence of flow around the airfoil)
These are also included in the AL-Transient/constant folder, and are called in the fvOptions code for that case, but they're also included here for ease.
If more Re values are desired, you have to go to Sheldahl and Klimas (1981) to find the Re values at all angles of attack. https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/6548367 In this, you'll find a wide range of Cd and Cl data for the Re values for the NACA 0018 airfoil. And this is the only place you can find em for 180 degrees of motion. Trust me, I've looked... Unfortuantely, since it's a scanned pdf that uses typewriter font, ChatGPT can't automatically transcribe the values into a table for you. So that's on you, buckaroo. Have fun typing out alllll those data points, I certainly did 
